      "sequence_position": 13,
      "problem": "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0.4 & 0.2 & 0.2 \\\\ 0.3 & 0.4 & 0.5 \\\\ 0.3 & 0.4 & 0.3\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}0.2 \\\\ 0.6 \\\\ 0.2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider a Markov chain with the stochastic matrix $P$ and the initial state vector ${x}_{0}$ given above. Calculate the state vector ${x}_{1}.$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the state vector ${x}_{1},$ we apply one step of the Markov chain:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=P{x}_{0}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =P{x}_{0} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0.4 & 0.2 & 0.2 \\\\ 0.3 & 0.4 & 0.5 \\\\ 0.3 & 0.4 & 0.3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0.2 \\\\ 0.6 \\\\ 0.2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0.24 \\\\ 0.4 \\\\ 0.36\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
